Why isn't this a simple adverbial use of the word for "sudden" as it appear=
s to be?  There is in English a displacement for some kind of emphasis, but=
 that is handled differently in Lojban.  The other question is, what is mea=
nt here?  The sense seems to be "out of the blue, without an anticipatory e=
vent, unexpectedly" and so might be the kind of transition that could be su=
mmed up by a discursive (which are not very clearly defined), but the simpl=
e adverb needs to be discounted before going on in this way.  =20




